LORE.push(
  {ch:538, n:'What Rheon Sees', t:'Rheon helped Mirelle reorganise her contacts and routes for hours and genuinely tried to understand her work. For the first time he saw her not as a mysterious woman he once met but as someone whose life and purpose he deeply respected. "You make this less lonely."'},
  {ch:539, n:'What Cannot Be Used Against You', t:'The Whispering Mask attacked the party openly with Shame, Doubt, Silence and Distrust. Each member acknowledged rather than denied the truth used against them: "They do not get to decide my worth." The Evil\'s power began to crumble as its secrets stopped working as leverage.'},
  {ch:540, n:'The Price of Silence', t:'The party learned the Whispering Mask had fed for years on communities too afraid to speak. Jade saw that killing it would not be enough: the conditions that sustained it, fear, shame and silence, had to be broken as well. Mirelle and Sally began preparing an information counterattack on two fronts.'},
  {ch:541, n:'Open Secrets', t:'Sally\'s Rumour Network and Mirelle\'s surviving contacts released carefully chosen truths through music, traders, couriers and servants. False blackmail collapsed, victims learned they were not alone, and the Whispering Mask began to lose strength as the fear of exposure fell. "We protect people through knowledge. We break their power through openness."'},
  {ch:542, n:'No More Leverage', t:'Jade led the confrontation with the Whispering Mask. Devon and Mirelle dismantled its information trap, Sally turned its rumours against it, Levi closed its escape routes, Sky protected its victims and Rheon fought as a frontline guest, repeatedly shielding Mirelle without being ordered to. With its leverage gone and the fear sustaining it collapsed, the Evil broke apart.'},
  {ch:543, n:'The Network Without a Master', t:'After victory Mirelle refused to rebuild the old network exactly as before. The new one used small independent cells, regional contacts, limited information sharing and no single master ledger, and was safer precisely because nobody controlled all of it.'},
  {ch:544, n:'Veyne Network', t:'Mirelle became a permanent Information Ally and named her new network the Veyne Network: no single ledger, no central control, independent regional cells that know only what they need to know. It complements Sally\'s Rumour Network, and belongs to everyone who takes part, not to her. "Information is power, but it should protect, not control."'},
  {ch:545, n:'The Prince Who Stayed', t:'With the formal mission over, Rheon had every reason to leave and stayed another day. He told Mirelle it was not politeness: staying was a choice, because he wanted to spend more time with her. For the first time she saw that his interest was no longer one-sided.'},
  {ch:546, n:'Who Devon Became', t:'Mirelle told Jade privately that Devon had changed more than he realised, not in title but in who he was when no one was watching. Jade expected a dramatic revelation; Mirelle simply said: "He trusts people now." It lands harder than anything else she could have said.'},
  {ch:547, n:'Someone Worth Knowing', t:'Later, when the others had withdrawn, Rheon told Mirelle that she was worth understanding, and that none of the things others saw in her, remarkable, capable, extraordinary, were why he wanted to know her. No confession followed and no title was given, but the direction was clear.'},
  {ch:548, n:'Home With Someone', t:'Jade told Devon she had enjoyed meeting someone who knew the person he used to be. Asked whether Mirelle had revealed anything embarrassing, she answered "Several things", then "Nothing I didn\'t like." Their marriage remained steady, comfortable and secure: "I\'m glad we get to come home to each other."'}
);

/* ---- Arc XXI, chapter 518: The Network Before Jade ---- */
LOCATIONS.capital.spots.push(
  {id:'hz518a', kind:'investigate', n:'You Had All This', icon:'🗺️', ch:518, need:2, ambush:[], lo:96, roles:['jade', 'devon'],
   desc:'Jade is surprised.',
   clues:['Jade learns more about Devon\'s old information system. Before he travelled with her, he had already built quiet connections across Dragonvale and nearby territories. Jade: "You had all this... before we even started travelling together?" Devon: "I didn\'t do it alone. I had people I trusted."', 'Before he met Jade, Devon moved quietly, building connections in Dragonvale and neighbouring territories.'], rw:{xp:601100, gold:122520}},
  {id:'hz518b', kind:'investigate', n:'A Small Circle of Trusted Contacts', icon:'🕯️', ch:518, need:2, ambush:[], lo:96, roles:['jade', 'devon'],
   desc:'His network.',
   clues:['He avoided attention, kept to the shadows, and relied on a small circle of trusted contacts. His network included merchants, informants, travellers, and people in unexpected places.', 'The map shows the links across Dragonvale, Northreach, Caelis, Redmere, Stormmere and the Western Isles.'], rw:{xp:601400, gold:122580}, needFlag:'inv_hz518a', lockMsg:'🔒 Finish the previous clue first'},
  {id:'hz518c', kind:'investigate', n:'One of the People He Trusted Most', icon:'🌸', ch:518, need:2, ambush:[], lo:96, roles:['jade', 'devon'],
   desc:'Mirelle.',
   clues:['Mirelle was one of the people he trusted most. She helped him with information, contacts and routes across multiple regions.', 'He shared what he needed to, but never everything. Even with his closest allies, he kept his own secrets.'], rw:{xp:601700, gold:122640}, needFlag:'inv_hz518b', lockMsg:'🔒 Finish the previous clue first'},
  {id:'hz518d', kind:'investigate', n:'Another Part of the Man I Married', icon:'💞', ch:518, need:2, ambush:[], lo:96, roles:['jade', 'devon'],
   desc:'A glimpse.',
   clues:['He was more cautious. Less trusting. More politically detached. But already highly capable.', 'This gives Jade a glimpse of Devon before their marriage: who he was, what he valued, and how much he had already built on his own. Jade: "I\'m not jealous. I\'m fascinated. It\'s like discovering another part of the man I married."'], rw:{xp:602000, gold:122700}, needFlag:'inv_hz518c', lockMsg:'🔒 Finish the previous clue first'},
);
