LORE.push(
  {ch:571, n:'Delilah', t:'Roc looked at Delilah not as the woman who "won" or a consolation prize but as the person who actually remained beside him: through his fall from status, exile, Liora, rebuilding, marriage, pregnancy, work and the ordinary ugliness of starting again. She had shared not just his victories but the worst of it, and she had never left.'},
  {ch:572, n:'The Woman Who Stayed', t:'At Dee Manor Roc thanked Delilah properly and admitted he had not always been a good husband. She answered "I\'m aware", told him to be better tomorrow and the day after, and, when he said it had taken him a long time to understand, "It took you long enough." Then she went back to her paperwork.'},
  {ch:573, n:'The King\'s Last Days', t:'As Aster\'s father failed rapidly and the court prepared for succession, the faction that had weaponised the twinhood made a final attempt: Roc is older, Devon may have an equal claim, Aster\'s marriage proved his support weak. The brothers stood together publicly instead, and the House presented a united front.'},
  {ch:574, n:'Devon\'s Choice', t:'Before the court Devon said he had no intention of claiming the throne: not because he had been defeated or pushed aside, but because he chose the life he already had. Jade, the road, his family and his own work. He gave Aster his full support. Not a crown, but a future of his own making.'},
  {ch:575, n:'Roc\'s Choice', t:'Offered the throne one final time, Roc refused: his path did not lie in the capital but at Dee Manor, with Delilah, Liora, the twins and the life he had rebuilt after losing everything. He gave Aster his full support, and the faction trying to divide the brothers had nothing left to work with.'},
  {ch:576, n:'The Crown Passes', t:'Aster\'s father died of his illness and the kingdom mourned its late king. Aster ascended the throne, younger than the age once imagined for him but no longer unprepared: he had served in the field, handled frontier affairs, managed court disputes and governed in his father\'s place. For the first time Jade and Devon bowed to him as King of Dragonvale.'},
  {ch:577, n:'The King Stands', t:'Aster addressed the court for the first time as king and spoke for himself: the frontier agreements would be upheld, trade and military protection would continue, and the dispute over Roc and Devon would not destabilise his reign. Jade, Roc, Devon, Elise and Fen stood behind him. House Xuanji had a king, and the succession crisis ended.'},
  {ch:578, n:'Elise\'s Question', t:'Aster\'s ascension changed Elise\'s situation at once: the frontier no longer depended on keeping a Crown Prince tied to her house, and as king he could guarantee it directly. The marriage had accomplished what it was created for. Elise loved Tarin and was already living two lives, and now had to ask whether she wanted to continue the public one.'}
);

