LORE.push(
  {ch:581, n:'Back on the Road', t:'After the House Xuanji crisis Jade\'s party rode out on what sounded like a simple field report: villages near the Frostveil Range reported snow far outside the normal season, and then the messages stopped. No caravans, no messengers, no word in over two weeks.'},
  {ch:582, n:'Snow in the Wrong Season', t:'In the lower Frostveil settlements the party found streams freezing overnight, animals fleeing downhill, failed crops and impassable roads. Jade suspected one of the Fifteen Evils but refused to declare it without evidence, and chose to question the villagers first.'},
  {ch:583, n:'The Village Beneath Ice', t:'The party found a village repeatedly buried by snow: no monster, only food, fuel, medicine, shelter and blocked roads. Jade ordered it stabilised before any hunt for the cause. By night the shelters were secure and supplies gathered, and the people had a chance to survive.'},
  {ch:584, n:'Sally\'s Warm Room', t:'Sally turned the village hall into an information centre with hot drinks, food and music. Her Rumour Network pieced together that the winter began near an old mountain shrine: several expeditions went up and very few returned, and those who did come back were injured, delirious or silent.'},
  {ch:585, n:'Levi\'s Trail', t:'Levi read the missing villagers\' tracks: people who knew the mountain well had left the safe path for a dangerous one. "They don\'t look like people who got lost by accident." He began marking a secure route along the ridge with red ribbons, and the party prepared to head for the old mountain shrine.'},
  {ch:586, n:'Sky\'s Patients', t:'Sky treated frostbite, exhaustion, dehydration and respiratory illness with ordinary medicine and spiritual healing, and noticed a strange cold residue in many patients\' spiritual circulation that ordinary medicine could not ease. It pointed to the mountain shrine.'},
  {ch:587, n:'Jade\'s Rule', t:'When local fighters wanted to march straight to the shrine, Jade refused and stated her rule: investigate first, judge second, destroy only when necessary. "Evil" does not always mean "kill immediately"; some have reasons, contracts or roles in a larger balance, and killing without understanding can make things worse. The village agreed to follow it.'},
  {ch:588, n:'The Shrine That Froze', t:'At the abandoned shrine the fires still burned but gave no heat, snow fell inside enclosed rooms and metal froze at a touch. It was the first undeniable supernatural sign: the shrine was abandoned, but whatever remained there was not natural.'},
  {ch:589, n:'Endless Winter', t:'The Fifteen Evils tracker named the presence: the Endless Winter, active, beneath the mountain and expanding. There was no giant creature, only something draining heat from the land, and its frozen territory grew larger every day. Jade: "We cannot stop it by force alone."'},
  {ch:590, n:'The People Who Fed It', t:'Old records showed that generations ago nearby communities kept seasonal offerings of food, herbs and crafted items around the mountain, to maintain a balance with something beneath it. The custom was forgotten as people migrated, and the winter began only after the last ritual site fell into disuse.'},
  {ch:591, n:'Not a Sacrifice', t:'A surviving fragment seemed to demand a human life, but Jade rejected that at once. Sky found that in the old healing language the same word can mean living warmth, vital breath or circulating energy: the ritual had been mistranslated and no human sacrifice was ever required.'},
  {ch:592, n:'Five Fires', t:'The party found five old beacon sites across the mountain: the Summit Fire (Sky Ember), West Fire (Stone Heart), East Fire (Wind Path), South Fire (Life Spring) and North Fire (Deep Earth). Together they once formed a circulation network that carried heat and spiritual energy. Restoring all five became the main objective, and none required human sacrifice.'},
  {ch:596, n:'The Fourth Went Dark', t:'The fourth beacon was lit and then went dark again: something beneath the mountain was actively resisting the restoration. "It pushed back. This is not a passive defence." The party realised the Endless Winter was aware of them.'},
  {ch:597, n:'Whiteout', t:'A violent storm struck and separated the party. Visibility dropped to almost nothing, and cold, exhaustion and disorientation became the real enemies as each of them fought alone to survive the whiteout.'},
  {ch:598, n:'Find the Voices', t:'In the whiteout Sally realised visual signals were useless and used sound instead: music and repeated rhythmic calls became navigation markers, and the separated party members followed them back to one another. Her musician background saved lives again.'},
  {ch:599, n:'Fourth Fire', t:'The party returned to the fourth beacon together and reinforced it with the circulation principles Sky had discovered at the third site. The beacon held. Four fires now burned across the Frostveil Range.'},
  {ch:600, n:'The Fifth Fire', t:'The final beacon lay closest to the mountain core. Lighting it revealed the true design: the five beacon sites formed a giant spiritual circulation system. They had never been weapons. They were part of the mountain\'s natural balance.'},
  {ch:601, n:'Why Winter Never Ends', t:'The party learned that the Endless Winter was once part of the natural seasonal cycle: it absorbed excess cold and released it gradually through the mountain network. Something disrupted that cycle generations ago and it became unable to release what it absorbed, so it kept taking more until winter stopped ending.'},
  {ch:602, n:'Destroy or Restore', t:'Jade faced the central decision: destroying the entity would stop the immediate threat but might permanently damage Frostveil\'s climate and spiritual balance, while restoring the circulation was harder and more dangerous. She chose restoration.'},
  {ch:603, n:'Into the Heart of Winter', t:'The party descended beneath the shrine into the frozen mountain core, a dungeon of ice, ancient channels and broken spiritual conduits. Each had a clear role: Jade lead and seal work, Devon protection and frontline control, Sky circulation and healing, Levi beacon targeting and ranged support, Sally disruption, information and evasion.'}
);

