LORE.push(
  {ch:611, n:'Back to Dragonvale', t:'The party came home to a changed Dragonvale: Aster settling into kingship, Elise increasingly absent from court, Fen moving freely between the archives, scholarly offices and court, and Jenika working heavily at the Pavilion. Sky saw at once that she was not entirely well.'},
  {ch:612, n:'The Imperial Pavilion', t:'The Pavilion serves the kingdom through medical care, research and healing, for the royal family, the court and the people of Dragonvale. Jenika, the Royal Cousin and senior Imperial Physician, is responsible for its administration, logistics, difficult cases and royal patients, with other healers, apprentices and attendants working under her. It never sleeps.'},
  {ch:614, n:'Valen Resonance', t:'Old records describe a rare resonance that appears to respond to Valen-related bloodlines and may bring a stronger healing affinity or an unusual sensitivity to curses and ancient energies. The Valen line is fragmented, with many names missing, deliberately or lost over time. Sky\'s response to it is a clue, not proof, of who his father is.'},
  {ch:615, n:'Elise\'s Illness', t:'The court believed Queen Elise ill: servants had seen her vomiting, tiring easily, eating irregularly and withdrawing from public appearances. Only a small inner circle knew the truth, that she was pregnant, and kept it private while she rested.'},
  {ch:616, n:'The Life Elise Wants', t:'Elise told Aster she did not want to remain trapped in a political marriage she never chose. Aster said she owed it to no one and the frontier no longer needed it. Tarin waited at the frontier, prepared to disappear with her, and Fen stayed in the palace quietly to see to her needs.'},
  {ch:617, n:'Aster\'s Solution', t:'Aster proposed that Queen Elise die, not truly but publicly: a medical record, a documented decline and a final diagnosis, so her political identity would end with her and no faction could find, use or manipulate her, or challenge Fen\'s legitimacy later. Only a small inner circle could know.'},
  {ch:618, n:'Two Women, One Height', t:'Elise and Fen are almost exactly the same height, and Aster is highly skilled at disguise. With a golden wig, jewellery and makeup in Elise\'s style, but Fen\'s own eyes, she could be plausible at a distance during carefully controlled appearances. Fen does not need to become Elise, only to preserve the illusion that Elise remains in the palace.'},
  {ch:619, n:'The Two Disguises', t:'Aster stripped away Elise\'s recognisable appearance (jewellery and cosmetics removed, hair dyed black and/or cut shorter, clothing, posture and mannerisms changed) and gave Fen an Elise-style wig, makeup, royal clothing, posture coaching and restricted speaking appearances, convincing enough from a distance.'},
  {ch:620, n:'Fen at Court', t:'Fen made her first controlled appearance as Elise: walking briefly, acknowledging a few officials, speaking minimally and retiring early. The court saw a visibly weakened queen, and the illness story became more believable.'},
  {ch:621, n:'The Road Out', t:'Elise left Dragonvale secretly with Tarin, her final disguise supervised by Aster, with Jade and Devon securing the route. By the time ministers noticed Queen Elise no longer appeared at court, the real Elise was already far away.'},
  {ch:622, n:'The Queen\'s Rest', t:'The palace announced that Elise\'s condition had worsened and suspended non-essential visits. The Pavilion\'s staff had already seen genuine symptoms, so the announcement drew little suspicion, and Jenika oversaw the medical bureaucracy from the physicians\' notes without examining the queen herself.'},
  {ch:623, n:'What the Cure Requires', t:'Jenika\'s research showed her curse was deep-rooted, binding body, spirit and vital energy, and that breaking it required extremely close physical and spiritual synchronisation with another person. Jade made clear Sky was under no obligation; Sky chose it, saying he wanted her to live.'},
  {ch:624, n:'The Curse Breaks', t:'Sky aligned his Valen resonance with Jenika\'s breath, pulse and spirit, and the curse that had bound her body, spirit and vital energy slowly broke. Their intimacy was part of the healing and of their existing feelings for one another, not a spectacle. Jenika survived, free of the curse.'},
  {ch:625, n:'Morning', t:'Sky woke before dawn and checked Jenika\'s pulse, breathing and temperature again and again, until she told him to stop checking whether she was alive. He checked once more anyway.'},
  {ch:626, n:'No Wedding Required', t:'Sky assumed they should marry; Jenika did not. They are together, their bond real without a ceremony, and neither considers marriage necessary to make it so. Their future stays unconventional, and they chose each other freely.'},
  {ch:627, n:'The Queen Declines', t:'Fen made her final controlled appearance as Queen Elise, coughing fake opera-troupe blood and ending the audience early. The court took it as proof her health was deteriorating, and the appearances stopped; the official account said she could no longer receive visitors.'},
  {ch:628, n:'Queen Elise\'s Death', t:'Dragonvale announced the death of Queen Elise after a prolonged illness, and the kingdom entered 49 days of official mourning. The story was believable because many servants and attendants had witnessed her genuine symptoms. Far from Dragonvale, Elise was alive.'},
  {ch:629, n:'Somewhere Else', t:'Far from Dragonvale, Elise lives with Tarin under her new look and identity, her hair dark and cut shorter, no one bowing and nothing expected of her, with her pregnancy continuing. Her old life is officially dead.'},
  {ch:630, n:'The Wedding Nobody Announces', t:'Aster and Fen travelled quietly to the frontier, dressed as ordinary travellers, and married privately under a flower canopy in a quiet village, with no banners, speeches or announcements. Jade\'s group, Roc and Delilah, and Elise and Tarin were there. It mirrored Aster\'s political frontier marriage to Elise, but this time he chose his wife, and she chose him.'}
);

