LORE.push(
  {ch:636, n:'Back on the Road', t:'The canon five left Dragonvale with Fen publicly Queen and Aster\'s court stabilising. Sky resumed travelling while Jenika stayed at the Pavilion, not knowing she was pregnant. Sally was glad to be moving again, and Levi remarked that she had lasted surprisingly long in court.'},
  {ch:638, n:'The Silence', t:'In the mountain village no sound could be produced: a worker fell from a roof unheard, a child wandered toward danger with no one able to shout, and a cooking fire spread silently. Sky found the villagers\' throats unharmed. Something was suppressing vibration throughout the area, and the loss of sound itself was becoming lethal.'},
  {ch:639, n:'Sally Without Music', t:'In the silenced village Sally sat with her instrument and did not play: her fingers rested on the strings but no audible note came. Devon and Levi were unsure what to say, but even in silence her presence was impossible to ignore.'},
  {ch:640, n:'The Old Beacon Road', t:'The party followed an ancient route through the mountains and found traces of a long-forgotten beacon network that once carried warnings between settlements during the old conflicts. One beacon was said to carry messages farther than ordinary flame; its name, the Silent Flame, appears repeatedly in the records.'},
  {ch:641, n:'Things That Move Quietly', t:'Creatures adapted to the silence moved without sound; attacks could not be heard and warnings could not be called, so Jade could not issue normal commands and Sky could not hear his allies\' cries. Levi\'s tracking, reading tracks, movement patterns and disturbed snow, became invaluable.'},
  {ch:642, n:'Silent Command', t:'Levi taught the group basic field signals: Stop / Hold, Move Forward, Split / Take Position, Hide / Stay Low, Spread Out and Fall Back. Sally mocked them at first, then saw how useful they were. In silence-zone encounters the party relies on visual signals, positioning, predetermined commands and companion instincts.'},
  {ch:643, n:'Rhythm Without Sound', t:'Sally found that although sound disappeared, physical vibration remained faintly detectable. Resting her hand against the body of her instrument, she could not hear the note but could feel it, and that became the foundation of her counter-technique.'},
  {ch:644, n:'The Bell That Never Rings', t:'The party found an enormous ancient warning bell that moved without sound. An inscription below it described the old beacon network: the Silent Flame once absorbed voices and carried their warnings across great distances, and originally people gave it words voluntarily.'},
  {ch:645, n:'Someone Fed the Fire', t:'During wartime, rulers forced the beacon to carry ever more powerful messages. Voices were magically extracted, and eventually entire communities were used to strengthen it. The Flame learned to take rather than receive: a beacon of willing voices became a system that consumes people, growing stronger with every voice.'},
  {ch:646, n:'The Ninth Shadow', t:'The Imperial records confirmed that the Silent Flame is one of the Fifteen Evils, the Ninth Shadow. Unlike the Endless Winter, its current existence depends on stealing something from living people: it originally received voices willingly and over time learned to take. Its power grows as more people are used, which makes it far more dangerous to abandon. Jade did not yet decide whether it could be restored.'},
  {ch:647, n:'Levi\'s Trail', t:'Levi followed faint ripples in the air that marked where the Flame had passed; without sound, tracking became almost entirely visual. Sally followed beside him, and their coordination was so natural that they barely needed signals anymore.'},
  {ch:648, n:'You Understood Me', t:'Sally spotted movement in the distance, but Levi was already moving before she gestured. He told her she did the same with him: "You show it in your eyes, your pace, and the way you hold your instrument. I can read it." Their relationship had reached the point where silence did not stop them communicating, which Sally found more romantic than she wanted to admit.'},
  {ch:649, n:'The First Voice', t:'A preserved testimony from the first person whose voice was forcibly given to the Flame: "I gave my voice so that others might live... I did not know then that it would never be mine again." The original beacon was never inherently evil; people changed what it was allowed to become, until voices were extracted and entire communities used to strengthen it.'},
  {ch:650, n:'What Restoration Would Cost', t:'The beacon\'s core mechanism showed the Silent Flame cannot exist in its present form without consuming voices, and that even its original function required living offerings: there is no harmless state to return it to. Jade decided the Silent Flame must end.'},
  {ch:651, n:'The Silent Furnace', t:'The party descended into the ancient beacon complex called the Silent Furnace. The silence became absolute: no dialogue, no spell calls and no warning cries. The way down is told through pictures alone.'},
  {ch:652, n:'The Flame That Makes No Sound', t:'The Silent Flame burned brilliantly with no crackling, no roar, no collapsing stone and no audible combat. Its presence suppresses every vibration around it.'},
  {ch:653, n:'The Silent Flame, Fought', t:'The fight against the Silent Flame has four phases: Stolen Voices (Silent Command), Heat Without Warning (Levi reads the safe paths), The Rhythm Beneath (Sally\'s vibration timing) and The Beacon Core (Jade reaches the original mechanism and destroys the system that let the Flame feed on living voices).'}
);
