LORE.push(
  {ch:667, n:'The Bone River', t:'An elder of a forgotten village recognised the old name: the Bone River once carried the dead toward a place where damaged life could be preserved: broken bodies mended and kept until they could be made whole again. It was a river of return and restoration, never meant to destroy, and its meaning has been forgotten for generations.'},
  {ch:668, n:'The Rule of the Network', t:'The restoration network can reconstruct tissues and move a body, but it cannot restore a soul that no longer exists: it cannot resurrect the truly dead. What the Bone River does is preservation, not resurrection: the river carried remains toward a place where damaged life could be preserved, and the movement it produces is movement without life.'},
  {ch:669, n:'The Pearl Pulls', t:'For the first time in years the Black Pearl reacted strongly, pulling Devon toward the river\'s source. It felt different from anything before: not just an Evil, but something much older than this civilization.'},
  {ch:670, n:'The Old Channel', t:'Levi found that the river once flowed through a completely different route: old maps and terrain records showed stone channels far older than the current settlements, deliberately sealed. Someone diverted the water centuries ago, with a deliberate plan that took both engineering and magic. The original channel still exists, sealed and forgotten.'},
  {ch:671, n:'The Preservation Complex', t:'Beneath the riverbed the party found ruins matching the Sunken Kingdom\'s preservation architecture: the same design language and purpose. They were preservation facilities, not for resurrection but for maintaining bodies, repairing damage and storing them. The Bone River was once part of a much larger system.'},
  {ch:672, n:'The River Was a Vein', t:'An inscription explained that the river did not merely carry water: it carried restorative energy between distant sites, one of the network\'s living conduits, functioning like a vein. It was a lifeline, a river that carried more than water, it carried life itself.'},
  {ch:673, n:'Something Woke It', t:'The network began activating without anyone commanding it. Devon\'s Pearl was not causing the awakening but responding to it: a receiver, not a trigger. Energy flowed through dormant channels and multiple sites reactivated at the same time. Someone had awakened the entire network, and not by accident; Jade was worried by the distinction.'},
  {ch:674, n:'The Dead Are Not the Enemy', t:'The animated remains were pulled by the damaged network toward restoration points. Destroying them would not help, since they would re-form, and breaking the flow without releasing it would only leave the energy to accumulate elsewhere. Sky developed a controlled release technique to disperse the residual energy: it calms the remains, and they slowly fall apart.'},
  {ch:675, n:'Release the Dead', t:'Remains at the Bone River can be fought when hostile, stabilized when unstable, or released: freeing the trapped restorative energy moves them on and recovers more restoration resources than destruction, a Restoration Shard, River Essence or Preservation Material.'},
  {ch:676, n:'The Village Beneath the Water', t:'Under the old channel the party found a drowned village in the Sunken Kingdom\'s preservation style, where a real community had lived. Its people died during the original sealing of the network, the Bone River absorbed their remains, and their unresolved presence eventually twisted the conduit.'},
  {ch:677, n:'Why the River Became Evil', t:'The Bone River was originally neutral, a natural conduit carrying restorative energy between distant sites. Centuries of death, sealed energy, corrupted flow and failed reconstruction attempts turned it into one of the Fifteen Evils: it now continuously tries to restore what cannot be restored. It was never meant to hold the dead.'},
  {ch:678, n:'Inherited Resonance', t:'For the first time Devon felt a fragment of inherited resonance as the Pearl pulled him toward the deepest chamber: not memory and not possession, but recognition of what the place once was, a network, a living conduit, a promise to heal and connect, whose pain now called to him.'},
  {ch:679, n:'The Custodian\'s Door', t:'A sealed chamber opened only when Devon approached with the Pearl. Its inscription read: "The bearer carries the Pearl until the network calls it home." It was the first explicit confirmation that Devon is a custodian, not the final owner. His friends answered that a custodian still matters and that they would walk the path together.'},
  {ch:680, n:'Nothing Is Surrendered', t:'Jade objected to the inscription\'s suggestion that Devon must give up the Pearl because destiny says so: a prophecy is not an order, just one possible future. Devon agreed. \'Home\' might mean a restored state, or Devon might be the one who decides when it returns. Devon keeps the Pearl, nothing is surrendered, and the choices along the way are still theirs.'},
  {ch:681, n:'The Heart of the Bone River', t:'At the corrupted restoration core the Bone River manifested as a massive serpentine formation of water, bone and ancient preservation energy. It was not malicious: it simply could not stop trying to repair the dead, gathering them, holding them and trying to put them back together, a never-ending attempt, a river that could not let go.'},
  {ch:682, n:'The Bone River, Fought', t:'The fight against the Bone River has four phases: Drowned Remains, Broken Current (the arena shifts as the channels change), Reconstruction (the river rebuilds what is destroyed) and Sever the Failed Loop (Sky identifies the corrupted cycle, Devon stabilises the Pearl resonance and Jade severs the loop).'},
  {ch:683, n:'Let the Dead Stay Dead', t:'Jade destroyed the corrupted reconstruction mechanism and Sky released the trapped restorative energy. The remains finally became still and the Bone River collapsed back into ordinary water. The Bone River was resolved: ten of the Fifteen.'},
  {ch:684, n:'The River Flows Forward', t:'After the Bone River was resolved the original watercourse slowly returned, and the restored energy travelled outward through ancient channels. Dormant structures began reacting across distant regions: a sealed archive in the Northern Reaches, forgotten terraces in the Eastern Valleys, a sunken gate in the Western Expanse and a hidden reservoir in the Southern Isles.'},
  {ch:685, n:'Something Is Connecting', t:'Devon\'s Pearl pulsed as, far away, an old shrine responded, a forgotten seal flickered, ancient waterways began moving and restoration sites briefly awoke. Sky saw that the Bone River was not an isolated system but one piece of something enormous. The restoration network was waking, and ten of the Fifteen stood resolved.'}
);
